ios: touch gestures (long-press on hold, right-click mode, proportional camera)

- Long-press opens the right-click menu WHILE HOLDING: after lcHost.settings.longPressMs (default
  450 ms) with the finger still within TOUCH_SLOP (10 CSS px) and no drag/camera pan started, the
  client right-clicks under the finger and asks the host for a 'medium' haptic. Releasing over a menu
  option picks it (press-drag-release); releasing anywhere else leaves the menu open for a tap; the
  release itself never clicks. Upstream right-clicked only on release after 500 ms, with no feedback.
  A long-press whose timer was starved by a busy main thread is still honoured on release.
- Tap path: if lcHost.takeSecondaryClick() returns true (host "right-click" mode), the tap clicks
  with button 2.
- A tap clicks only once a frame has been drawn at the finger's position. What a left click does is
  the top entry of the minimenu, which each draw rebuilds from mouseX/mouseY (3D picking included). A
  mouse hovers before it clicks; a quick tap can lift before any frame was drawn there and would run
  the previous spot's action (60 ms taps on "Accept" did "Cancel" in headless Chrome). When needed the
  click is deferred by one frame (flushPendingTap); otherwise it is immediate as before.
- Camera drag in the 3D view is proportional: yaw/pitch follow the finger delta (4 yaw / 2 pitch
  units per CSS px, times lcHost.settings.cameraSensitivity), pitch clamped to 128..383, no momentum,
  sendCamera set so EVENT_CAMERA_POSITION reports it. Upstream held arrow keys like a joystick, so the
  camera kept spinning while the finger rested. Touches therefore no longer hold or release arrow keys
  (which also stops a canvas touch from cancelling keys the host holds for on-screen buttons).
- Side/chat drag emulation starts after TOUCH_SLOP instead of 5 px so a slightly wobbly long-press on
  an inventory item is not taken for a drag.

